Tools: [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "initialize_git_repository", "description": "Initialize a new Git repository in the specified project path.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"project_path": {"type": "string", "description": "The file system path to the project where the Git repository will be initialized.", "enum": [null]}, "editor": {"type": "string", "description": "The code editor being used for the project.", "enum": [null]}}, "required": ["project_path"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "create_branch", "description": "Create a new branch in the Git repository and optionally check it out.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"branch_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the new branch to create.", "enum": [null]}, "checkout": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Whether to checkout the new branch immediately after creation.", "enum": [null]}}, "required": ["branch_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "commit_changes", "description": "Commit changes to the Git repository with a specified commit message.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"message": {"type": "string", "description": "The commit message describing the changes.", "enum": [null]}, "files": {"type": "array", "description": "A list of file paths to include in the commit.", "items": {"type": "string"}}}, "required": ["message", "files"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "push_to_remote", "description": "Push committed changes to a remote Git repository.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"remote_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the remote repository to push changes to.", "enum": [null]}, "branch_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the branch to push changes from.", "enum": [null]}}, "required": ["remote_name", "branch_name"]}}}]\nExample: I will help you set up the Git repository, create the feature branch, commit your initial files, and push the changes to the remote origin. Here are the necessary steps executed via function calls:

<tool_call>
{"name": "initialize_git_repository", "arguments": {"project_path": "/Users/myusername/projects/my-application", "editor": "Visual Studio Code"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "create_branch", "arguments": {"branch_name": "feature-branch", "checkout": true}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "commit_changes", "arguments": {"message": "Initial commit", "files": ["/Users/myusername/projects/my-application/initial-files"]}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "push_to_remote", "arguments": {"remote_name": "origin", "branch_name": "feature-branch"}}
</tool_call>

Tools: [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "ExpertQAExtractor", "description": "Extracts a list of questions that focus on summarizing a specific topic found in the document.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"topic_summarization_questions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}}, "required": ["topic_summarization_questions"]}}}]\nExample: <tool_call>
{"name": "ExpertQAExtractor", "arguments": {"topic_summarization_questions": ["What are the fundamental differences in purpose and approach between Aristotelian and Rogerian argumentation models?", "How does the concept of 'multipartiality' redefine the goal of neutrality in academic writing?", "What are the specific rules of critical engagement in pragma-dialectics, and how do violations of these rules constitute logical fallacies?", "In what rhetorical situations is an Aristotelian approach more effective than a Rogerian one, and vice versa?", "How do the Freedom Rule, Burden-of-Proof Rule, and Standpoint Rule function to ensure ethical argumentation?"]}}
</tool_call>

Tools: [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "ExpertQAExtractor", "description": "Extracts a list of questions that focus on summarizing a specific topic found in the document.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"topic_summarization_questions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}}, "required": ["topic_summarization_questions"]}}}]\nExample: <tool_call>
